        "id": "q-1792341402531-120",
        "text": "Dwight, as Security Lead, perform a comprehensive security audit and implement high-level hardening across the entire GyftKart project:\n\nStep 1: Codebase & Dependency Audit\n- Read the entire project tree, review package dependencies for vulnerabilities (`npm audit`), and verify all environment variable handling.\n- Ensure that NO secret keys (like SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or admin secrets) are exposed to client-side Vite bundles (`VITE_*` prefix leak).\n\nStep 2: Supabase Database & RLS (Row Level Security) Hardening\n- Audit every table: `profiles`, `b2b_profiles`, `upi_payment_sessions`, `wallet_transactions`, `orders`, and `brands`.\n- Verify RLS is enabled (`ALTER TABLE ... ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`) on every table.\n- Strict Policy Enforcement:\n  - Users can ONLY read and write their own data (`auth.uid() = user_id`).\n  - No direct client-side UPDATE or DELETE access on `wallet_transactions` or `upi_payment_sessions`.\n  - Only authorized admin sessions (`is_admin = true` or verified admin service role) can perform updates on payment approvals, reverts, and company ledger.\n\nStep 3: Frontend & API Guarding\n- Input sanitization against XSS and injection attacks on search bars, UTR inputs, and forms.\n- Enforce strict Content Security Policy (CSP) and HTTP security headers (X-Frame-Options: DENY, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, Referrer-Policy).\n- Add frontend client rate-limiting on wallet submission, UTR verification, and login forms to prevent brute-force abuse.\n- Report all verified security measures in `SECURITY.md`.",
        "ts": 1792341402531
      }
    ]
